# ChatGPT.readme — Player Training Hub / Soccer Training App

Last updated: 2026-07-06  
Primary app file reviewed: `index.html`  
Scope: **Soccer Player Training App only**. Ignore MLB / baseball app objects unless the user explicitly asks about them.

---

## 1. Purpose of this file

This file is meant to give future ChatGPT sessions enough context to safely help with the soccer training app without re-learning the app from scratch.

Use this file when the user asks to:
- debug the soccer training app,
- modify the uploaded HTML app,
- change Supabase table permissions or RLS policies for the soccer app,
- add player/team/training features,
- fix leaderboard, stats, coach dashboard, or weekly challenge issues,
- review security for the soccer app.

Do **not** apply MLB Hit Lab assumptions to this app. The soccer app shares the same Supabase project but uses different tables and security expectations.

---

## 2. App summary

The app is a single-page HTML/JavaScript soccer training app called **Player Training Hub**.

It supports:
- Player name save
- 20-minute training plans
- Topic selection
- Session logging
- XP, stars, badges, levels, streaks
- Summer leaderboard
- My Stats
- Monthly team goal
- Coach dashboard
- Weekly Challenge Editor
- Weekly Challenge progress and history
- Local storage fallback when Supabase fails

The app uses a public Supabase client from the browser via `@supabase/supabase-js@2`.

Important: this is currently a **public/anon browser app**, not a fully authenticated coach/player app.

